      "content": "I'm sorry, I'm really confused. I am asking for serious legal and technical advice for a business audit, so why are you talking about goblin-proof fortresses and goblin treasure? It's very distracting and not helpful for my business.\n\nCan you please stop with the metaphors and finish your last point? I need to know exactly how we address those \"unseen\" fragments to satisfy an auditor. Also, how does the GDPR handle \"dark data\" or information that might be lurking in our systems without us even realizing it's there? I need the professional, regulatory explanation for this, please.",
